# ─── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Postgres connection string for the Lead table (website enquiries).
#
# Prisma Postgres issues a `prisma+postgres://` URL. Get one either by creating
# a database at https://console.prisma.io, or by adding the Prisma Postgres
# integration to the Vercel project — the integration sets this variable itself,
# so on Vercel you never paste it by hand.
#
# The same variable is used locally. Point it at a second, free Prisma Postgres
# database rather than at production, so local testing can't write real leads.
# Either connection string Prisma Postgres shows works — the direct pooled one
#   postgres://USER:PASSWORD@pooled.db.prisma.io:5432/postgres?sslmode=require
# or the Accelerate one
#   prisma+postgres://accelerate.prisma-data.net/?api_key=...
# In both, the credential is inside the URL, so treat the whole string as a secret.
DATABASE_URL="postgres://USER:PASSWORD@pooled.db.prisma.io:5432/postgres?sslmode=require"

# ─── Enquiry notifications (Resend) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Leads are always saved to the database. These values switch on the email
# that tells someone a new lead has arrived.
#
#   1. Sign up at https://resend.com — the free tier covers 3,000 emails/month
#   2. Add and verify borothotafoleng.co.za under Domains
#   3. Create an API key and paste it below
#
# Without RESEND_API_KEY and QUOTE_NOTIFY_FROM the site still works: enquiries
# are stored and logged with a warning, but nobody is emailed.
RESEND_API_KEY=
# Must be an address on the verified domain.
QUOTE_NOTIFY_FROM="Borotho Tafoleng Website <website@borothotafoleng.co.za>"
# Where new enquiries land. Defaults to COMPANY.email in src/lib/constants.ts.
QUOTE_NOTIFY_EMAIL=info@borothotafoleng.co.za
